iality map\n<MATH_0018> in <MATH_0019>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nThese data are subject to the following conditions\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(i)<ITEMCLOSE_0001>\nin the situation of (<REF_0003>) the diagram\n<MATH_0020>\nis commutative in <MATH_0021>,\n<ITEMOPEN_0002>(ii)<ITEMCLOSE_0002>\ngiven <MATH_0022> as in (<REF_0004>) and <MATH_0023>\nsetting <MATH_0024> and <MATH_0025> the\ncomposition of the functoriality maps <MATH_0026> and <MATH_0027> is\nthe functoriality map <MATH_0028>,\n<ITEMOPEN_0003>(iii)<ITEMCLOSE_0003>\nthe maps of (<REF_0005>) are isomorphisms\ncompatible with the functoriality\nmaps and the maps of Remark <REF_0006>,\n<ITEMOPEN_0004>(iv)<ITEMCLOSE_0004>\nthe composition <MATH_0029>\ncorresponds to the canonical element of\n<MATH_0030>, see\nRemark <REF_0007>,\n<ITEMOPEN_0005>(v)<ITEMCLOSE_0005>\ngiven a deformation situation <MATH_0031> with <MATH_0032>\nthe composition <MATH_0033> is zero in\n<MATH_0034>\nif and only if <MATH_0035> lifts to <MATH_0036>.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:038178881ddfc0efa11e57a1031355b0f1444f24979a0256c41630556ae19b58", "unit_id": "tag:07YP:statement"}
